# Run H (2026-11-06, user: "SAC + in-loss cloning"): run F
# (il_finetune_c0_sac_pin_dims.env: SAC, noise pinned at c0's level per action,
# il_data + il_data_cover, LayerNorm critic, frozen trunk, 1000 critic-only
# online updates) with the cloning term INSIDE the SAC actor loss, TD3+BC style:
#
#   alpha_T log pi - (2.5 / mean|Q|) Q(s, pi(s)) + mean((tanh(mu(s_E)) - a_E)^2)
#
# on one optimizer, a_E the expert's clean labels (torch_rl/gated_recurrent_tqc.py,
# commit 2f5e9cb). Why: the separate cloning step ran on its own Adam, which
# ignores a loss's scale, so its weight never held the clone, and every SAC run
# followed the critics' tilt (left + less throttle in every expert state, which
# the expert-bias reward check showed the reward does not want). 2.5 is TD3+BC's
# published default. In this mode il_finetune_prepare takes no separate cloning
# step, and this cloning term does not fade.
. "$REPO/slurm/il_finetune_c0_sac_pin_dims.env"
export ACTOR_BC_ALPHA=2.5
